### 4. Treasury Payments & Cash Movement Platform

*Senior Full Stack Developer · .NET 8, EF Core, React 19, TypeScript, ag-Grid Enterprise, Kyriba, Azure Service Bus, FluentValidation*

Built the payment approval and execution platform managing all cash movements between investors, deals, and funds, routed through the Kyriba treasury system.

- Designed a unified payment lifecycle (create → approve → route to treasury → funded) specialized across nine payment types, including investor drawdowns (Collections), distributions (Return of Capital), leverage utilizations, inter-account transfers, and operational expenses.
- Implemented dual-state payment tracking separating internal fund-treasury approval status from external treasury execution status, keeping the two workflows independently auditable.
- Built the two-phase Kyriba integration (forecast submission → payment execution) with asynchronous status callbacks via message queues, alerting, and job orchestration.
- Developed multi-fund payment splitting (one parent movement fanning out to per-fund child payments) and flexible cross-currency/cross-fund routing for non-standard cases, backed by an FX rates service with monthly-average rates for reporting.
- Exposed a secured integration API allowing external loan-management systems to create and amend payment forms programmatically, with policy-based authorization and beneficiary amount-sum validation.
- Delivered cash movement summary dashboards with ag-Grid Enterprise, including advanced filtering, saved user grid profiles, and KYC/beneficiary validation rules at every approval boundary.

